[[:db/add "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87" :answer/id #uuid "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87"] [:db/add "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87" :answer/value "-1"] [:db/ensure "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87" :answer/validate] [:db/add "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/id #uuid "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4"] [:db/add "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/choices "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87"] [:db/add "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/correct "ef4830d4-fe84-50ea-ae37-82464c7b5b87"] [:db/ensure "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/id #uuid "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a"] [:db/add "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/ff/ff715081614305046275762dd5e00f8650a710c492282f0efda17222b46fdb73.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/worked-solution "First trace $4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/60/604217b82feab6efde2dab25bc17716ad7c57cf9f4dbb1a36dadeb5e8dcf2a11.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $4$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{4}{4}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=4\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/answer-fields "cf413c98-6009-592b-a945-886a70e2a9f4"] [:db/ensure "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "1b819296-16a5-5a72-9afd-23e06c588b9a"] [:db/add "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311" :answer/id #uuid "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311"] [:db/add "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311" :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{4}"] [:db/ensure "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311" :answer/validate] [:db/add "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272" :answer/id #uuid "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272"] [:db/add "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272" :answer/value "-4"] [:db/ensure "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272" :answer/validate] [:db/add "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c" :answer/id #uuid "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c"] [:db/add "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c" :answer/value "-\\frac{16}{5}"] [:db/ensure "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c" :answer/validate] [:db/add "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555" :answer/id #uuid "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555"] [:db/add "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555" :answer/value "-\\frac{15}{4}"] [:db/ensure "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555" :answer/validate] [:db/add "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37" :answer/id #uuid "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37"] [:db/add "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37" :answer/value "-16"] [:db/ensure "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37" :answer/validate] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/id #uuid "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/key "selection"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/choices "31a839c0-3231-58f6-902c-8d69ebdea311"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/choices "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/choices "61362677-9732-5595-b71f-bfaa70cbed2c"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/choices "644e9ad1-abc3-5761-a63d-d25bc1df0555"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/choices "24ea3843-7b62-52af-9b94-41a2cb5acf37"] [:db/add "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/correct "63bafe55-8647-50d5-b37b-2f916471a272"] [:db/ensure "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/id #uuid "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2"] [:db/add "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/fc/fca4a9bf588f65a3b71f5c1f8c015cbb62f2215db89d931c23e8145ebb7fbdc4.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/worked-solution "First trace $3\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/c8/c800221aa90828b720c568766c9099c92e5cb3e15c323515783d327a1df633c8.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $16$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{16}{4}=4$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-4\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=3\\mathbf{b}+(-4\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+3\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-4$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/answer-fields "47d0ee29-6c91-5e8d-9935-7795fa57912a"] [:db/ensure "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "f52a731f-c7f1-5305-99d3-8750263968c2"] [:db/add "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6" :answer/id #uuid "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6"] [:db/add "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "2d06382d-3e17-589c-875a-e6c3ee7a43e6" :answer/validate] [:db/add "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac" :answer/id #uuid "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac"] [:db/add "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac" :answer/value "-6"] [:db/ensure "aae16f3e-532c-5878-ae0d-b275f139ddac" :answer/validate] [:db/add "1f00eade-f4fa-5b6c-8f55-8438c8af9751" :answer/id #uuid "1f00eade-f4fa-5b6c