:question/id #uuid "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691"] [:db/add "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/8b/8be6c345d59432ae56d1f819173299150727f88ccabee44b8323019e3faa683e.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691" :question/worked-solution "First trace $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/ec/ecc5dc46a0abbd1a7b2c1abbde5e15f410402d25169d50e88c1c16c81d55d081.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $4$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $16$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{16}{4}=4$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-4\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}+(-4\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-4\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-4$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691" :question/answer-fields "b6f8e68e-d38c-5a53-8ea1-46b3c3f3430a"] [:db/ensure "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "f5b09c94-a00c-5b53-926a-a3c811085691"] [:db/add "74039efb-7bb3-50fe-a367-48da2ebb8372" :answer/id #uuid "74039efb-7bb3-50fe-a367-48da2ebb8372"] [:db/add "74039efb-7bb3-50fe-a367-48da2ebb8372" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "7