nswer-field/choices "04e59e71-c3a3-531c-be5b-e8e1539159c6"] [:db/add "878cf631-17ec-5e55-8129-1f701829df47" :answer-field/choices "820a98c4-0e47-5497-b8ae-51f072a43703"] [:db/add "878cf631-17ec-5e55-8129-1f701829df47" :answer-field/choices "3b00023b-a88a-59ea-86ef-3eabc5796ae9"] [:db/add "878cf631-17ec-5e55-8129-1f701829df47" :answer-field/correct "04e59e71-c3a3-531c-be5b-e8e1539159c6"] [:db/ensure "878cf631-17ec-5e55-8129-1f701829df47" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/id #uuid "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b"] [:db/add "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/da/dae364c9c1ca2df27876c1524f4b94dfb49f0081ebec249f698dbe08dd186ea7.png)\n\nGiven $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$, find $\\lambda$."] [:db/add "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/worked-solution "First trace $2\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/d4/d43ce8711cf587ab4552b74961da61f8829f9540d9bab507ee7cf127b6494068.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $3$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $3$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{3}{3}=1$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=2\\mathbf{b}+(-\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-1$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/answer-fields "878cf631-17ec-5e55-8129-1f701829df47"] [:db/ensure "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "abea290f-68e0-521f-9d44-bf4f5d85f63b"] [:db/add "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4" :answer/id #uuid "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4"] [:db/add "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4" :answer/value "-3"] [:db/ensure "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4" :answer/validate] [:db/add "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/id #uuid "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5"] [:db/add "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/key "field-1"] [:db/add "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank] [:db/add "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/choices "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4"] [:db/add "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/correct "b83df11c-3a84-563b-9421-de4af8d7b6d4"] [:db/ensure "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5" :answer-field/validate] [:db/add "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/id #uuid "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3"] [:db/add "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/problem "The three vectors share an origin, and each grid square has the same side length.\n\n![](images/5f/5f3e3731fd7465240ac96d6cb891dc928227714dfe38016da65be2b7aa70709d.png)\n\nIf $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$, then $\\lambda=$ {{field-1}}."] [:db/add "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/worked-solution "First trace $4\\mathbf{b}$ from the common origin $O$ to a point $P$: keep its direction and scale its length. The remaining path from $P$ to the endpoint $C$ must be the unknown multiple of $\\mathbf{a}$.\n\n![](images/3c/3cb061b20184edf057ed7d3e2a933cd63c522f51b8ee8e8628ddecd9ea87005d.png)\n\nFollowing the grid direction of $\\mathbf{a}$ takes $2$ steps, while the parallel path $PC$ has $6$ steps. Their length ratio is $\\frac{6}{2}=3$. The remaining path points in the opposite direction to $\\mathbf{a}$, so\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{PC}=-3\\mathbf{a}.\n$$\nAdding the path vectors gives\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathbf{c}&=\\overrightarrow{OP}+\\overrightarrow{PC}\\\\\n&=4\\mathbf{b}+(-3\\mathbf{a})\\\\\n&=-3\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\nBecause $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ are nonparallel, these coefficients are unique. Comparing with $\\mathbf{c}=\\lambda\\mathbf{a}+4\\mathbf{b}$ gives $\\lambda=-3$. The minus sign records the reversed direction."] [:db/add "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] [:db/add "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/answer-fields "f8557e34-1bf2-5bd0-9874-6a84871e48b5"] [:db/ensure "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/questions "4e70f560-6b6e-5f2a-9639-2d8e015ed0c3"] [:db/ensure 17592186235285 :knowledge-point/validate]]
